{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And from Bamot.</b> They spread out to <b>the valley</b> called in the portion of Mas'ei 'the valley of Shittim'; and 'valley' (גיא) and 'Abel' mean a plain and steppe." "<b>Which is in the field of Moab, head of the peak.</b> This refers back to the word ומבמות, meaning: that height which is in the field of Moab — it is <b>head of the peak, looking out over the face of the wilderness</b>; that is the great desert. <b>Which is in the field of Moab.</b> Because originally it belonged to him [Moab], he calls it by his name, and likewise 'plains of Moab.' Another interpretation: <b>And from the wilderness, Mattanah.</b> There is great significance in that well, for from the wilderness — a place of thirst for water — it was given to them as a gift (מתנה)." "<b>And from Mattanah, Nahaliel.</b> It was not like other wells that flow in their own place, but once He gave it to them it gathered strength and became a great stream (נחל). And the yod is superfluous in it, like היושבי בשמים, המגביהי, המשפילי. And 'El' means strength, like ואת אילי הארץ לקח, and so it is written: ויצאו מים רבים." "<b>And from Nahaliel, Bamot.</b> And once it became a stream from the abundance of water, the stream continued and spread beyond the heights, and from the heights that <b>are in the field of Moab</b> — which is head of the peak looking out over the face of the wilderness — the stream of the well descended into the valley."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:06.437132925Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}